  "folders": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Get Started & Test Cards",
      "desc": "## Get started here\n\n**60-second tour:** open **03 - Ecommerce Checkout → 1. Purchase** → **Send** → **Visualize tab** → click **Open payment page →** → pay with a test card below → back here, send **Check Transaction** → APPROVED.\n\nThe full guide lives on the collection **Overview** tab (click the collection name). Nothing needs configuring — the public sandbox demo merchant is pre-filled.\n\nThis folder: test cards, endpoints reference, and the docs links.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "0. Get Started (60-second walkthrough)",
          "method": "GET",
          "url": "https://developer.payway.com.kh/overview-865678m0",
          "hasPre": false,
          "hasTest": false,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Sandbox Test Cards",
          "method": "GET",
          "url": "https://developer.payway.com.kh/resources-3305682f0",
          "hasPre": false,
          "hasTest": false,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reference - API Endpoints List (doc)",
          "method": "GET",
          "url": "https://developer.payway.com.kh/api-endpoints-984508m0",
          "hasPre": false,
          "hasTest": false,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 - Ecommerce Checkout",
      "desc": "## Ecommerce Checkout\nREST endpoints for the standard hosted-checkout flow (cards, ABA KHQR, wallets).\n\n**Suggested order:**\n1. **Purchase** - creates a transaction and returns a hosted page; save the `tran_id` (auto-stored in `{{last_tran_id}}`).\n2. **Check Transaction** - fast status check while a customer pays (great for polling).\n3. **Get Transaction Details** - full record.\n4. **Close Transaction** / **Refund** - close or money-back (Refund needs RSA).\n5. **Transaction List** / **Exchange Rate** - admin views.\n\nAll hashes follow `req_time + merchant_id + tran_id + ...` per endpoint (see each description).",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "1. Purchase (Hosted Checkout) - multipart",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/purchase",
          "bodyMode": "formdata",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Get Transaction Details",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/transaction-detail",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Check Transaction (fast, recent)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/check-transaction-2",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Close Transaction",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/close-transaction",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Refund - RSA merchant_auth",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/online-transaction/refund",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Transaction List (filter)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/transaction-list-2",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Exchange Rate",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/exchange-rate",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 - ABA QR API",
      "desc": "## ABA QR API\n`POST /generate-qr` creates an ABA KHQR for static/dynamic payment. Render `qr_data` as a QR image, or show `qr_image`. The payer scans with the ABA app.\n\nAfter payment, verify via **Check Transaction** or the callback. The purchase_type/payment_option both default to `{{payment_option}}`.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "Generate QR",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/generate-qr",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 - Payment Link",
      "desc": "## Payment Link\nCreate a shareable payment link (sent via WhatsApp/email/SMS) and query its stats.\n\n> These are **portal APIs**: instead of a plain hash they require `merchant_auth` = base64 of the RSA-encrypted payload. Install node-forge or paste a pre-encrypted value into `{{pl_merchant_auth}}`.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "Create Payment Link",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/payment-link/create",
          "bodyMode": "formdata",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Payment Link Details",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/payment-link/detail",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "06 - Pre-auth",
      "desc": "## Pre-auth (Card holds)\nPre-authorisation flow: after a `purchase`, complete (capture) or cancel the hold. Use `pre-auth-completion` optionally with a **payout** split.\n\nOrder of fields in the hash differs per request - read the description before editing values.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "1. Complete Pre-auth",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/online-transaction/pre-auth-completion",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Complete Pre-auth with Payout",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/online-transaction/pre-auth-completion",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Cancel Pre-auth",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/online-transaction/pre-auth-cancellation",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "07 - Payout",
      "desc": "## Payout\nMass payouts (up to 250 beneficiaries) plus the whitelist that authorities them.\n\n**Sequence:** whitelist the payee account first, then send a payout. Both need RSA (folder 06 variables). Payout hashes use the **body beneficiaries ciphertext** as a hash input, so the hash must be computed AFTER encryption.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "1. Payout (to beneficiaries)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v2/direct-payment/merchant/payout",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Add Account to Payout Whitelist - RSA",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/whitelist-account/add-whitelist-payout",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Update Payser Status - RSA",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchant-portal/merchant-access/whitelist-account/update-whitelist-status",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "08 - Credentials on File (CoF)",
      "desc": "## Credentials on File (CoF) / Subscriptions\nTokenize a card or ABA account, then charge it later without re-entering credentials.\n\n**Typical flow:** `1. Link Account` (or `2. Link Card`) -> wait for callback -> `3. Get Token Details` (auto-saves `{{pwt}}`/`{{ctid}}`) -> `4. Payment` -> `6. Remove` at the end.\n\n`callback_url` must be base64-encoded in the hash/body - the scripts do that automatically for https URLs. Run `7. Subscription` to test recurring CITR_FIX payments.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "1. Link Account (ABA Account)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-credential/v3/aof/link-account",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Link Card (Credit/Debit)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-credential/v3/cof/link-card",
          "bodyMode": "formdata",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Get Token Details",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-credential/v3/token-management/get-token-details",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Payment (Using Token)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v3/purchase/payment-credential",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Renew Token (ABA account)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-credential/v3/token-management/renew-expired-account-token",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Remove Token (irreversible)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-credential/v3/token-management/remove-token",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Subscription (Scheduled Payment)",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/purchase",
          "bodyMode": "formdata",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "09 - KHQR Guideline",
      "desc": "## KHQR guideline\nUse a dedicated `instore` QR merchant account. Generate a QR (folder 04), have the payer scan it, and look up the matched inbound transaction with the merchant reference you set.",
      "requests": [
        {
          "name": "Get Transactions by Merchant Ref",
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/payment-gateway/v1/payments/get-transactions-by-mc-ref",
          "bodyMode": "raw",
          "hasPre": true,
          "hasTest": true,
          "snr": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "10 - Callbacks & Webhooks",
      "desc": "## Callbacks & Webhooks\nEverything PayWay POSTs back to **your** server, plus how to verify it.\n\n- Set `{{callback_listener}}` (e.g. webhook.site) and these sample senders will POST real-looking payloads to it.\n- The `X-PayWay-Hmac-Sha512` header is computed with the same ksort+concat rule PayWay uses, so you can test your verifier end-to-end.\n- 'Webhook Design Notes' summarises idempotency / retry / response guidance.\n\n## How to get a callback URL\nPostman has no built-in inbound URL; you provide one.\n\n1. **Free webhook catcher (easiest)** - open **webhook.site** (or webhookbin.com), copy its `https://webhook.site/<uuid>` URL, and paste it into `{{callback_url}}`, `{{cof_callback_url}}` and `{{callback_listener}}`. PayWay/sample senders will POST results there and you watch payloads arrive in the browser.\n   - While PayWay does not push straight into Postman, you **can sync webhook.site -> Postman**: webhook.site exposes a REST API. `GET https://api.webhook.site/token/<uuid>/requests` returns every received payload as JSON. A dedicated Postman request can call that endpoint and, in its test script, save `pwt`/`ctid`/`tran_id` from the latest callback into collection variables - effectively importing the callback. (webhookbin has no such API; use webhook.site for the sync trick.)\n2. **Postman Mock Server (closest Postman-native)** - create a mock server for this collection in the Postman web UI; it issues a public `https://<mock-id>.mock.pstmn.io` URL that accepts any POST and returns your mock response. The **Call Logs** tab shows every received callback (headers + body) so you can read `pwt`/`tran_id` there.\n3. **ngrok + local listener** - `ngrok http 8080` pointed at a local web server; set `{{callback_url}}` to the ngrok URL. Best when you want to script saving variables or run a verifier locally.\n\n> Tip: for the CoF workflows (folders 08 / 11) the callback is optional - request `3. Get Token Details` already fetches and saves `pwt`/`ctid` from the API using `{{request_id}}`.",
      "requests": [
